        "id": 4840250
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-05-28T16:05:58Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Thanks for the concern, The intent here is to enforce post-init kernel text/rodata integrity from El2 using S2 permissions (This comes as a part of FLEX requirement from AUTO), not to add generic ACK policy. The protection values comes from EL2 being outside EL1\u0027s write authority after layout is frozen.\n\nIntroducing a vendor specific hook will expand the kernel attack surface, since the information is security sensitive and consumed only once by Gunyah EL2, we are trying to keep handoff tightly scoped.",
